  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "Kalle's special – passing and an overlap",
  "description": "Line A in one corner by the goal, line B further out on the other side, and a fixed passer (C). The cones are by the centre line.\n\nStep 1: A passes diagonally to the first in line B, then skates down along the board and around the cone. B passes to A as they round the cone, and A passes back to B, who has taken a step forward from the line.\n\nStep 2: B passes to the fixed passer C. Right after the pass, A and B make an overlap – they cross each other's paths in towards goal. C passes to one of them, who shoots.\n\nTeach step 1 first, then add step 2. Rotate A–B–A, and change the fixed passer now and then. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Pass in the skating direction so the receiver can keep their speed."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "At the overlap: skate close to each other so the defence struggles to choose."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "C: look up and pick whoever is most free."
    }
  ],
